WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.440
A widow follows her only son's
coffin out of the town of Nain.

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.340
Without him, she has no protector.

3
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:10.800
In Luke's story, Jesus
touches the coffin and says:

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.830
Young man, I tell you, arise!

5
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.310
Luke tells of healings, a
storm calmed, and a crowd fed.

6
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:24.540
In 1748, David Hume set a very high
bar for believing any miracle report.

7
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.180
So why does Luke tell these stories,
and can a modern reader believe them?

8
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.370
In this mission, you'll
explore 5 miracle stories,

9
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.970
from a dying servant to a storm.

10
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.180
Then you'll weigh up the
sceptics, and the replies.

11
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.820
Your mission: find out why
Luke tells miracle stories,

12
00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.590
and weigh up whether a modern
reader can believe them.
